  .12E6 Keeps BC
  .12E7 DE = the text, HL = the block
  .12E8 Look up every element
  .12EA Read and walk the path
  .12ED Failed?
  .12EF Anything after the path?
  .12F0 Error $A8

@12F2 DIR_SELECT_POP
  Part of DIR_SELECT: puts BC back; returns an error (NZ).
  .12F2 BC back

@12F4 DIR_SELECT_GO
  Part of DIR_SELECT: starts the search at the directory's first entry; Z.
  .12F4 Start at the first entry
  .12F7 Z: done

@1356 PATH_PARSE_DEF
  PATH_PARSE_BLK with drive 0 (the default).
  Entry: A = the parse flags (IX+6); C = PATH_PARSE's flags; DE = the text.
  Exit: as PATH_PARSE.
  Error: as PATH_PARSE.
  Changes: AF, BC, DE, HL, IX, IY, AF', BC', DE', HL'.
