feedback missing 1005 The card does not say the entry's address ($D005) is passed at $01CA to $03DF, which stores it as the RAM disk's driver; nor the same for $1FD3 at $01B2. A "referenced as an immediate" fact would have saved a search of the ROM bytes.
feedback wrong 1FC5 The card runs $1FC5 on past its RET at $1FD2 into $1FD3-$1FEA, a separate entry (the floppy driver, address passed at $01B2); it should be its own card.
feedback wrong 154A $1581 is reported as a jump to $3F16, but it is reached only with Z (from $157F) so never jumps; its operand bytes hide LD D,$FF at $1582 (from $157A).
feedback pattern 1513-1546 PATH_GET_CHAR and PATH_UNGET_CHAR keep the text in the alternate set; every caller's register facts (BC', DE') follow from that, worked out by hand several times.
feedback listing 0F9C-0FD6 Opened to see what falls into $0FD6 (the key read and $BFF2 test) and $01A0-$01E0 for the $D005 reference.
question 1005 Does the code that calls a driver put the caller's page-1 segment back? RAMDISK_DRIVER leaves its own segment in page 1 and the caller's in A'.
